Title: DRY CROSSING
Author: Sam Whitaker
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. DRY RIVER CROSSING - DAY

Dust devils. A cattle herd bunches at a vanished ford. RANCHER HOLT MCCREADY, 50s, scans the cracked bed with binoculars.
HOLT
Water's gone upstream. We move or we lose half the herd by sundown.

EXT. RIDGE TRAIL - DAY

Holt rides with his foreman, JESSE, 30s. Below, the DAWSON spread — a dam of stacked river rock, new and deliberate.
JESSE
Dawson diverts the flow to his south pasture. Always wanted this crossing.
HOLT
Then we ask before we shoot.

INT. DAWSON RANCH HOUSE - DAY

WILL DAWSON, 45, boots on the table, rifle within reach. Holt stands in the doorway, hat in hand.
HOLT
Your dam's killing my cattle. Tear it down.
DAWSON
River changed course on God's timetable. I just helped.

EXT. DRY RIVER CROSSING - DUSK

Holt's crew attempts a drive across cracked mud. A steer breaks leg-deep. Gunshots pop — warning shots from Dawson's ridge.
JESSE
They're herding us, not the cattle!

EXT. DRY RIVER CROSSING - NIGHT

Holt walks the bed alone, lantern low. He finds a dynamite crate half-buried — not Dawson's mark. Someone else wants this fight bloody.
HOLT
Jesse, we got a third hand in this war. And he's lighting fuses.

FADE OUT.


THE END
